                Preface

In the journey of success, the adventures and experiences along the
path are more beneficial and vital, oftentimes, than the perks of arrival
at the destination. Thus, in the quest for success, the attributes and
attitudes one develops and what one becomes due to the demands of
the journey are more profound, lasting and beneficial than the things
one acquires for getting to the destination.

Like all journeys to the unknown, the value of a tour guide in the
journey of success is immeasurable. Wisdom is the principal guide in
the journey of life. At every point, Wisdom tells what to do, which way
to go, where to take a bend, when to halt, with whom to and not to
walk, and guides on many other crucial decisions in the course of the
journey. Wisdom prevents one from errors thereby increasing one’s
chances of safe arrival to destiny.

The Wisdom of God is the foundation upon which the entire universe
is built. Therefore, access to Divine Wisdom is like having the architect
who designed the plans of a very complex mansion to show one around
the building. One can not miss the way when the designer of the
blueprint is also the guide.
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

This book focuses on Wisdom particularly in the context of achieving
success in your life, vision, and destiny. The principles outlined are
both straightforward and deep, rooted in God's Word. The insights
shared in this book aim to motivate, push boundaries, spark creativity,
and illuminate the path for you to reach your full potential.
                                 CHAPTER 1

             Understanding Self-Discovery
                   and Self-Perception

Succeeding from the Inner Self

All true success flows from inside out. Success and greatness is more as
a result of internal attributes than external conditions. This is the
reason that two people can have exact external circumstances from
birth till adulthood and turn out with life outcomes as different as the
North pole from the South. It is a fact that two people can be born in
the same location, by the same parents, go to the same schools, taught
by the same teachers and one turns out a failure and the other a
success. Whenever this happens, then there is necessarily somewhere
along the life journey of such people that one must have got access to
certain information, people, event or things that conditioned his/her
inner realities differently from the other. If we carefully review the lives
of such people, we would be able to somehow somewhere account for
how the successful person made certain decisions or was exposed to
certain environments, people, information or events that constructed
his/her inner self differently from the failed people. The success or
failure of each of these persons in our study must definitely have flowed
from their inner realities.

                                                               1
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Thus, all endeavors at making people successful must target their inner
conditioning before their outward manifestation. The most important
elements in attaining success are discovering, developing and
actualizing one’s inner potentials. The talk about the absolute
importance of self-discovery and potential actualization seems to have
been reduced to mere motivational cliche due to common talk by
many. However, it is an eternal truth of life and cannot be disregarded.
You will only be able to live a life of meaning when you discover your
inner self and actualize your innate potential.

Therefore, investing in one’s inner self, mind and spirit through reading
empowering books like the one you are holding right now, acquiring
advantageous information, relating with right people, exposure to
enabling environments, developing superior thinking, beliefs,
paradigms and spirituality remain the timeless pathway to success.

The Myth of Self Discovery

Self discovery is the prerequisite for success and fulfillment in life.
However, the concept of self-discovery has been largely
misunderstood. The popular talk about self-discovery, especially
among secular speakers and environments many times, leaves people
more confused than oriented. This is because many of the self-help
theorems and strategies postulated seek to fix from outside an issue
that need to be addressed from the inner self.
To really understand the concept of self-discovery, we need to go back
to the first reference to the human-self in scriptures. In Gen 1:26-27,
God said,

                                                               2
                UNDERSTANDING SELF-DISCOVERY AND SELF-PERCEPTION

"Let us make man in our image, in our likeness . . . So God created man in
his own image, in the image of God he created him; male and female he
created them.

Humanity was made in the image and likeness of God - this truth is
fundamental to self-discovery. Believing anything less puts one at risk
of confusion. Primarily, being made in the image and likeness of God
talks about the fact that man (both male and female) was created a
spirit in the order and class of God. Thus, the God-nature, His DNA,
is in man by creation. Furthermore, being made in the image and
likeness of God implies that there is the revelation of God that is
fabricated into the created man which he is to reveal on earth. Thus,
there is something about God that every created person represents and
is to reveal to the world. Self discovery is simply knowing the
dimension of God that you were created to reveal to your world.

Before the fall of man in Genesis Chapter three, there was never a
discussion or need for self-discovery. Adam knew who he was, he knew
what each of the animals was by a glance and he knew who Eve was at
first sight. Adam and Eve knew that they were God’s regents over the
earth. They had a ‘default’ self-knowledge. Self discovery is simply
‘non-default’ self-knowledge. That is, taking a while to come to the
awareness of something about yourself that has always been there. Self-
discovery is a term used to describe knowing who you are and what
you were created to do - “truths that are at home with you all the
while”. This is where many worldly self-help trainers and their victims,
miss the rope.

                                                               3
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

They make self-discovery look like something people have to go to
search for. Thereby, they engage people into a gear of endless fruitless
search. Why do I have to go and look for me? Why do I need another
human to describe “me to me”.

At the fall, man lost connection with God and became confused about
his identity and purpose. The whole industry that has evolved around
self and purpose discovery was necessitated by “The Fall”. The entire
business and discourse of self-discovery are man’s attempt to look for
his identity and purpose. There are currently a lot of postulations on
how to know oneself, one’s abilities, purpose and life meaning by
experts and professionals in the multi-billion dollar self-discovery
industry. Truly, some of the tactics have some credit to them. However,
discovery of identity and purpose is simplified when one goes back to
God’s mind for the creation of man at the beginning.

You are the image and likeness of God - this is your identity. Of
course, the image and likeness of God is infinite and can not be
holistically expressed by human. Thus, God deposits a dimension and
revelation of Himself into everything He created to reveal. Even
inanimate objects have a particular revelation of God that are given to
reveal (see Psa 19: 1-4, Rom 1: 19 - 20).

Every human is different and are all created in the image and likeness
of God. This does not mean that God has multiple identities like one
suffering from identity crises, this rather shows that God is multi-
dimensional and every of His child is to display a dimension of God.

                                                               4
              UNDERSTANDING SELF-DISCOVERY AND SELF-PERCEPTION

God is many things - a parent, teacher, inventor, artist, scientist,
communicator, healer, entrepreneur, musician, leader, administrator,
writer, counsellor, king, lord and so on. Thus, whatever you are,
there is a dimension in God that resonates with that. Self discovery is
simply discovering the dimension(s) of God that is captured your
identity. This is achieved after you become connected to God
through faith in Jesus Christ and then by seeking God and allowing
Him to reveal to you the part of Himself that pertains to you. This
means that self-discovery, especially for a child of God, is actually
“God discovery”. Simply put, self is the discovering from God of the
dimension of Him that you were created to reveal to the world.
In scriptural doctrine, being created in the image and likeness of
God is talking about the fact that God is a Spirit and humans are
made a spirit like Him. However, it is absolutely important to know
that the image of God, in application and revelation, talks about the
varied dimensions of God that each of His child is to reveal in a
unique way.

This understanding explains why two different people can be
learning about God, reading the same Bible, being taught by same
teachers under the same conditions, seeking God under the same
environments, but are seeing different realities about God. This also
explains why it is unwise to make the entire pursuit of your life being
or doing what someone else is or doing, in a comparative or
competitive way.

                                                             5
                                           THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

 A teacher seeks God and finds doctrines, a business person seeks
God and finds practical business principles, a preacher seeks God
and sees sermons, and a musician seeks God and sees lyrics
overflowing in melodies, an intercessor seeks God and sees prayer
points, a leader/political inclined person seeks God and finds
governance. An inventor seeks God and finds creativity. A thought
leader seeks God and finds ideas. God is so vast and no one can
know all of Him and all about Him. A good way to know who you
are is to devote yourself to seeking God and see the revelations that
He gives you about yourself. God in His sovereignty actually
supervises the revelation of Himself that each person gets and makes
it to be according to the uniqueness of His assignment and destiny
for them. Thus, to discover yourself, first become connected to God
through faith in Jesus Christ, then decide to be and celebrate what
God created you to be. Also, be determined not to be intimidated in
appreciating the importance of the dimension of God you represent.

Thereafter, be committed to seeking God and discovering Him. The
only way to truly discover and know yourself is by seeking and
knowing God. When you seek God, you find yourself. In other
words, when you seek God, you find the particular dimension of
Him that pertains to your destiny. The secret of self confidence and
self esteem is loving, appreciating, celebrating and believing in the
importance of the dimension of God that you represent on earth.

                                                             6
              UNDERSTANDING SELF-DISCOVERY AND SELF-PERCEPTION

 A school teacher with this understanding reveals God with such
boldness as an Apostle over a Church congregation. After all, Jesus
was both referred to as an Apostle and a Rabbi in the Bible. Rabbis
are teachers in the Jewish culture, and the role is more akin to the
role of a contemporary school teacher than a pastor in today’s
culture.

The simple secret of self-discovery is to grow in the revelation,
understanding and character of God. The more you know Him, the
more you know yourself. After all, you are made in His image and
likeness. A lot of methodologies for self-discovery has been
promulgated by experts and motivational trainers. Some of these
strategies include ‘taking inventory of your weaknesses and
strengths’,‘identifying your pain and pleasure points’, ‘identifying the
things you do effortlessly and passionately’ and questions like ‘what
would you love to do even if you are not paid?’ are often used as self-
discovery tools.

While there is much credit and benefit to some of the self-help
methodologies engaged in the world, the eternal tools for self and
purpose discovery are an intimate walk with God, high investiture in
prayers and the Word, growth in spiritual understanding especially
about God’s Kingdom and the practical principles of life from God’s
perspective, learning to identify and hear God’s word and obeying in
faith the instructions of God per time. Walking with God in faith and
obedience leads along the path of destiny.

                                                             7
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

 The Question of Self-Actualisation

Obviously, some people would be quick to question the concept of self
discovery taught here and advocate that there are tons of Forbes
wealthy people, accomplished leaders, world’s successful figures,
Fortune 500 business owners, that have been conglomerates that do
not have a relationship with God and have discovered themselves and
succeeded. ‘How can you possibly claim the path to self-discovery is
God-discovery when many people who do not believe in God have
discovered their gifting and further utilised them to achieve
unprecedented success without God?’, they would ask.

Good questions produce good answers. However, there are some
questions that the answer is an entire understanding and body of
knowledge. The only way to get such answers is to be patient and open
enough to listen to adequate explanation which can only be
communicated by the body of teaching. The answer to comprehensive
answer to the above question is the mindset which this book would
have given as many as patiently and humbly learn to the end of it.

However, I will stimulate the questioning minds with three thoughts
while we journey through this book into an accurate understanding of
success, fulfillment and purpose and, therefore the full understanding
that answers the question in their minds.

                                                               8
                UNDERSTANDING SELF-DISCOVERY AND SELF-PERCEPTION

Point one; It is possible not to have a relationship with God and still
harness one’s most innate abilities and maximize its potentials in
achieving material success. However, true success and self-
actualisation is not merely material accomplishment. Hence, we can
not conclude that those category of people have succeeded until we
have understood what success is in the real sense of it. Understanding
success from a more accurate and higher perspective is a major theme
of this volume.

Point two; people can attain great material success by being aligned
with the principles that make for success without self discovery. This is
the reason you see some of them that are entrepreneurs build serial
businesses in different spaces and niches and fields and succeed in
them all. What is working for them is not self discovery but disciplined
alignment with the principles of productivity, wealth and material
success. Some highly successful people in a field have made statements
that insinuate they would still have succeeded irrespective of the field
they purpose. A contemporary accomplished leader in the Kingdom
frequently remarks that he would have been successful even if he was a
food seller. The truth is that diligence, focus, excellence, discipline,
skill and productivity and some other virtues in a person produce
material success irrespective of what they channel those virtues
towards. Understanding these virtues was the theme of Volume One of
Wisdom for Success. So, applying oneself to principles of success will
produce great material results but the dimension of success that lies in
fulfilling the essence of one’s life and existence is possible only by self-
discovery through God-discovery.

                                                               9
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Point three; thus, a holistic understanding of true success and self-
fulfillment, which is the aim of this volume, makes one realize that
many of the who are the reference points for material success without
self-discovery and self-actualization in God have neither truly
discovered self nor really succeeded. They have only material wealth
and human perception of success through compliance with the
principles of value, productivity, impact and wealth. True success and
self-actualization, when all is said and done, cannot be totally
appraised on this side of eternity.

                                                              10
                                 CHAPTER 2

              The Mystery of Self Perception

Another vital element in attaining success is accurate self perception.
After discovering who you are in God, it is important that you begin to
see yourself from God’s perspective. Self -perception talks about how
you see yourself, which in turn governs how you think, what you say
and your expectations from yourself and others. The first challenge of
success and fulfillment would be the challenge of developing an
accurate self-perception.

Jesus, at a crucial point during his earth-walk, asked His disciples, a
crucial question, “Who do people say that I am?”
He had before this time declared who He was, but the claims He made
about who He was did not go down well with some people. Even
though, He knew who He was, He still wanted to know what
perception of people about Him was. This was not so that He could get
His self-identity or self-definition from their perception, but so that He
could assertively correct the wrong perception about Him of people
closest to Him.

The truth is that people’s perception of you is important, especially the
people who are closest to you in daily life and work. People’s
perception of you affects your chances of success in many ways.

                                                              11
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Wrong, inappropriate or inadequate perception of your value by people
needs to be intentionally managed and possibly corrected. This is
because how people perceive you determines how they relate with you,
their expectations about you, the level of opportunities, honour and
rewards they offer you, their faith and investment into you, and their
support or resistance to your vision.

Jesus asked his disciples who people thought He was and they
answered by giving many inaccurate perceptions about Him. Truly, to
a large extent, people’s perception about you will be inaccurate and
less than your actual value. They perceived Jesus to be Elijah,
Jeremiah, John the Baptist, and some of these were great names. but
Jesus’ true identity and worth was far higher than all the mighty names
mentioned. This shows that even those that perceive you well. may not
perceive you as well as they should. It takes God for someone to
correctly see the infinite greatness of your potential. Thus, when Peter
perceived Jesus correctly, He quickly noted that this was only possible
because God revealed it to him. Indeed, no one can truly know the
vastness of your potential and destiny unless God tells it to them. So do
not feel despised when people see you less than you are. It is human to
perceive inaccurately, it is divine to perceive you correctly.

However, more important than other people’s perception of you is your
self-perception. In the Bible, Jewish leaders sent priests and Temple
assistants from Jerusalem to ask John the Baptist who he was.

                                                              12
                                   THE MYSTERY OF SELF PERCEPTION

Their question was a test of his perception of himself. They suggested
some identities which they wanted to put on him. They asked if he was
Eijah, the long-awaited prophet or the Christ. John simply replied
them, “I am the voice shouting in the wilderness . . .’’ It is important not
to leave your life definition to people, situations, circumstances or fate.
You need to know who you are and see yourself through the lens of
who you truly are.

John’s statement about himself was directly curled from the prophecy
that had been given about him by Prophet Isaiah centuries before His
birth. When asked who he was, He replied by giving the Word of God
that had been given about Him. The only accurate source of self-
perception is what God says about you. John defined himself in terms
of the Word of God for his destiny and not based on his situation,
profession or circumstance. It is wise not to define yourself based on
extrinsic possessions, circumstantial happening or any other ephemeral
standard. It is only right to define yourself only in terms of the
prophecy God has told you about your destiny. If your self-perception
is based on your background, bank balance, educational achievement,
job and professional or life circumstances, you will see yourself less
than you truly are. Obviously, what one sees in life is what one gets.
Seeing yourself less than you are will lead to under-achievement of
potential.

This is the reason you must define yourself by your future, vision,
destiny, life-assignment and God’s promise to you. When asked who
you are, answer based on who God has promised you will become.

                                                              13
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

The Question of Self-Actualisation

The only acceptable basis for your self-perception is God’s perception
of you. Not even your perception of yourself, outside of God’s word,
and certainly not others’ perception of you is accurate. It is only God
who truly knows your actual value. Everyone around will value you
wrongly; most times, below your actual value. You will, most certainly,
value yourself wrongly too– yes, below what you are worth. God’s
perception of you is always higher than everyone’s - including your -
perception of you .

God spoke to a young guy named Jeremiah, “before I formed you in the
womb I knew you, before you were born I set you apart; I appointed you
as a prophet to the nations.” However, Jeremiah’s perception of himself
was much less so he said “Ah, Sovereign Lord,” He said, “I do not know
how to speak; I am only a child.”
God saw him as an international leader, He saw himself as a child. God
saw him as a global voice, people saw him as a noise-maker, he saw
himself as someone with no voice. God needed to spend ample time
working on his perception of himself, before he could enter into his
destiny as an international prophet. A man can never rise above his
self-perception. Even God cannot make you successful if you
continually see yourself a failure.

God’s perception and definition of you is your true value. Who God
created you to be, what He made you to do and the destiny God
created to fulfill are what truly describes who you are. The first step in
developing a healthy self-perception, self-esteem and confidence is to
find out what God perceives and believes you to be.

                                                              14
                                   THE MYSTERY OF SELF PERCEPTION

Thereafter, correct your self-perception by adopting God’s perception
of you. Your Creator knows the capacity and ability of the human giga-
machine he fabricated, therefore, God has a gigantic perception of your
person and ability. Let this be the basis for your self-image, self-
identity, self-definition and self-belief. This will lead to a healthy self-
esteem. It will improve your perception of yourself, your productivity
and success.

In fact, let me throw to you the question that was thrown to John.
‘Who are you’?

