                                                            17
                                 CHAPTER 3

            Understanding Self-Definition

Definitions are always the first basis for clarifying and understanding
any concept. At all levels of schooling, whenever a topic is to be taught,
the teacher starts by giving a working definition of it. A good and
simple definition makes a concept well-understood, clear, easily
relatable and applicable. A vital part of understanding, discovering and
maximising your life purpose is to have a working definition of your
life. A life of impact starts with a clear and concise definition.

Self Definition is mentally articulating, verbally or textually expressing
what you believe your life is all about. Self-Definition is defining in
clear terms who you are and what you life is about. Self-discovery and
accurate self-perception should be followed by a succinct self-
definition.

Your self-definition should align with God’s perception of you. You
are not to define yourself by what you are going through or what you
do. Don’t be defined by your current state in life; your income, job,
status or environment. You are to be defined by what God had in mind
when He created you. You are who God says you are.

                                                              18
                                           THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

In making an eternal success out of your life, after self-discovery and
having aligned your self-perception with God’s perspective of you,
the next step in success is to have a working life definition for your
life.

John the Baptist was asked who he was, and he replied by giving
them his life definition. John replied in the words of the prophet
Isaiah: "I am a voice shouting in the wilderness, 'Clear the way for the
Lord's coming!'" (John 1:23). John quoted this statement verbatim
from the prophecy about his life in the Book of Isaiah 40: 3. Thus,
John knew the Word of God that had gone ahead of him and he
defined himself based on it. A vital foundation for understanding
your life-essence and purpose is having a word from God about your
life upon which you describe and define who you are. This is the only
sure foundation of self discovery, self-awareness and self-confidence.
Self-confidence comes from perceiving and believing in yourself from
God’s perceptive even when you do not look like it yet.

Your self-definition is the statement you hold as the description your
destiny, it is who you believe you are and what you believe you are to
do with your life, based on what God has revealed to you about your
life. It must be sourced in God’s promises, prophecies or scripture for
you. These scriptures you must have received, internalized, and
believed so strongly in your heart that it has become a concrete
consciousness and reality to your inner-self.

                                                            19
                                UNDERSTANDING SELF-DEFINITION

Your working definition of yourself must be so real to you that
contrary people, status, situations, and circumstances cannot make
you believe otherwise.

Life Scriptures

Furthermore, it is absolutely important that you have scriptures in
your spirit that you have received and are convinced that they are
direct descriptions of your destiny. The concept of having “Life
Scriptures” is different from the generic privilege of all believers to
appropriate the promises and blessings of relevant scriptures to areas
of need in their lives. While there is nothing wrong with a believer
scripture-shopping to claim promises or appropriate God’s word for
different areas of life, this is not the same as having a scripture or two
that you are convinced about that actually describes your life and
destiny. Such scripture(s) are not to be shopped for, but to be sought
for because they are given by the Holy Spirit to you specifically as the
prophecy of your life. Developing correct self awareness demands
praying extensively till the Spirit of God deposits your “Life
Scripture(s)” into your spirit. When you receive them, you hinge your
life on it and use them as the true North of the compass of your life as
you begin to align your consciousness and capacity development
towards that direction.

Currently, I have two scriptures that are in this category with me. In
this book, I will disclose one. Ps 105:22 says, “Joseph trained the
king's officers the way he wanted and taught his respected leaders
wisdom.” (KJV says taught SENATORS wisdom).

                                                            20
                                           THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Incidentally, I had not understood as much as I do now about my life
purpose, assignment and direction, when Psa 105: 22 has always, for
no obvious reason to me then, stood in my heart as a sign-post. I
wrote this scripture down in my diaries for years, my spirit leaps and
I prayed in the spirit each time I read it. I noted it in my spirit even
when I did not fully understand what it meant to me. It took more
than 10 years of knowing this was a life scripture for me, before I
began to get into the understanding of what the scripture represents
to me. Over a decade now, I have understanding that one of my
primary life assignments is raising and mentoring leaders and my
primary message is wisdom. So, basically in addition to the general
requirements and proficiency of ministry, which every Kingdom
believer, Christian minister/worker and Five-fold minister should be
apt in, I am particularly a teacher/trainer and my primary message is
