Write Your Life Statement

Find a quiet place and think about your life and develop an essential
definition for it. It is vital that your Life Statement is well articulated
and written down. An unwritten Life Statement is simply non-
existent, no matter how clearly it is conceived. It is also noteworthy
that a single statement as the ones listed above may not come so
easily for you. So, do not be too yoked with unnecessary
perfectionism in crafting a life statement. Just write what you believe
best describes what you know about your assignment for now and
start working with what you have. Life has a way of unfolding when
one is moving. Whatever you are able to write right now will do the
great job of getting you started.

Furthermore, you should note that Life Statements are dynamic;
what you write now may change with time as you understand more
about your life. The written Life Statement is like a picture on a wall,
far from sight as you move towards it, it becomes clearer and greater
details begin to unfold.

                                                            24
                                           THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Meditate and pray about your life in a secret place and write what
you believe describes your life essence for now. Do not be under the
