Life core values

It is important to define who you are and what your life is all about.
It is equally important to define what you stand for in life. There
must be crucial tenets upon which your life is founded. It is a true
saying that the person who does not know what he/she stands for,
would fall for anything. Life Core Values are the foundational codes
of ethics upon which one’s life is built on. They are the binding rules
of life which you hold as a strong conviction and have a
determination never to compromise. Having strong Life Values
brings stability, and consistency with eventual predictability to your
success in life. Great people are those who are prepared to stand for
their life values, even if they will have to pay a price for doing so.

Life Core Values must also be written down. When Life Values are
not predetermined and predefined, one will not be able to take a firm
stand at some crucial points when life presents conflicting
alternatives, compromising choices without prior notice. A lot of
people make decisions or take alternatives which they later regret
and wish they had not taken. Having Core Values that have been
practiced over years, helps constitute a strong and sometimes, semi-
conscious solid-cast mental system for decision making in daily
living.

Examples of some great Life Core Values include; ‘God-first-always’,
integrity, excellence, responsibility, self-reliance, financial
independence, productivity, delayed-gratification, fidelity, chastity,
morality, charity, kindness, friendliness, diligence, and many more
which you can develop.

                                                            27
                                UNDERSTANDING SELF-DEFINITION

 Do not make them too many so that you can imbibe them in
your consciousness. Write between three to eight and practice
