                                 CHAPTER 4

                  The Life Assignment

There is a reason you are on earth, there is a need you are created to
meet and a problem you are born to solve. Your Life Assignment is the
reason you were created and born. Genuine success is discovering,
training for, living and fulfilling your life assignment.
Success in today’s world has been mostly defined in terms of material
parameters. Material success have become not just a dream, but the
whole essence of life for many persons. However, viewing success from
a purely materialistic perspective is deceptive at best and dangerous at
worst. While real success comes with a level of material attainment, it
cannot be measured solely in terms of material possession. After
salvation, which secure eternal success, true life success is best
measured in terms of fulfilling one’s Life Assignment.

The Need You Were Born to Meet

Your Life Assignment is the need God created you to meet. God does
not do needless things and will not create anything without a need for
it. Even science agrees that everything, both animate and inanimate, in
the universe contributes a role to the sustainable inter-working of
nature.

                                                              33
                                           THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

A vivid example of this is in respiration, where plants breathe in
carbon dioxide to give off oxygen, which is taken in by animals to
give off carbon dioxide; which is in turn breathed in by the plants.
Also, in the biological system of living things, every part of the body
has a function it plays in the overall functionality. The vitality of the
heart, lungs, legs, hands and major organs are unquestionable, but
even seemingly insignificant parts have an assignment in the body.
Do you know that the hair on our body plays a role in insulation
against heat and the eyebrows keeps sweat of the eyes? Even the
appendix which has been said to play no role in the anatomy have
been discovered by experts to have served a role when human diet
was mostly vegetarian. Furthermore, more recent research has
shown that the appendix currently plays a role in the human immune
system. Nothing is created without purpose. God is very intentional
and detailed. He who creates seemingly insignificant things for
specific purposes and assignments, will definitely have a purpose for
man, the height of His creation, who was created in his image and
likeness.

From Adam and Eve, to every person thereafter, there is an existent
need each person is assigned to fill. Gen 1: 26 is the scripture where
man was mentioned for the first time in the Bible and it is in
reference with an assignment. It reads, God said, Let us make man in
our image, after our likeness: and let them have dominion over the fish
of the sea, and over the fowl of the air, and over the cattle, and over all
the earth, and over every creeping thing that creepeth upon the earth
(Gen 1:26).

                                                            34
                                           THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

This scripture shows that the creation of man was necessitated by an
assignment that God needed to be done - He needed someone to fill
the role of an administrator over all His creation. Thus, without the
need for a governor over the earth, there would have been no need
for the creation of man. Man, by essence therefore, is a creature of
assignment. This is one reason it is frustrating for people when they
having nothing to do. Humans naturally cope with having too much
to do, than with having nothing at all to do. We are created for doing
the assignment. Have you noticed how frustrated people are when
they are jobless and how self-destructive people become when they
