Pointers to the Assignment?
Some pointers have been popularly promulgated by self-help trainers in
discovering one’s life assignment. They emphasize the place of
knowing your abilities, discovering your passion and gifts, identifying
your heart-burden and painpoint. The heart-burden and painpoint is
generally used to describe the area where you have a heart-seated
concern for people and where you feel the weight of the wrongness of
things, so much that you want to make them right even if the wrong
doesn’t affect you directly, it is what and where you care enough to
want to address the issue.

                                                              41
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Motivational speakers ask questions like, ‘what would you like to do
even if you will not be paid for doing it?’ Someone once humorously
