Therefore, self-searching to discover these aforementioned pointers
and answering the questions are valid and important . However, these
pointers are not the path to assignment discovery. The way to
discovering life assignment like self-discovery, is hinged on vibrant and
close walk with God.

While it is beneficial to pay attention to your passion, gifts, burdens,
and pain-points. The great truth remains that your assignment is in
God and will unfold as a result of your walk with Him. These pointers
may not absolutely lead you to your life assignment.

The truth is that God can give you an assignment in an area where you
do not seem particularly to be gifted for and/or send you to a place you
do not have a passion to go. We have seen preachers that are not good
orators and business tycoons who do not seem smart. God loves to give
people assignments that make you always need Him and sends you to a
place where you will always be dependent on Him. Therefore, He can
give you things you seem not to be naturally gifted for to do. This is the
reason in identifying the Life Assignment, seeking God, not seeking
pointers, is premium. A formula, recipe or equation promulgated by
people for assignment discovery will not work, only the Spirit of God
can lead you into your life assignment.

