the Lord God had planted a garden in the east, in Eden; and there he put
the man he had formed. And the Lord God made all kinds of trees grow
out of the ground — trees that were pleasing to the eye and good for food .
. . The Lord God took the man and put him in the Garden of Eden to work
it and take care of it.

A logical question from the above scripture is, ‘how do you give a man
everything he needs for free and supply him with luxuries before you
give him work?’ Why does a man need to work when he already has
everything he needs? The Truth is, people today except those that have
an understanding of Life Assignment, will have no reason whatsoever
to work anymore if they were given all that Adam had in the Garden.
Giving man all he needs for food, shelter and satisfaction of needs,
before giving him work shows that God’s intention for creating work is
not as a means for having food to eat, an instrument of survival and a
tool for meeting material needs, however work was given to man for a
greater purpose.

The Working for the Purpose of the Assignment

Gen 2:5-7 &15 reads, “. . . No shrub of the field had yet appeared on the
earth and no plant of the field had yet sprung up, for the Lord God had not
sent rain on the earth and there was no man to work the ground . . . so The
Lord God formed the man from the dust of the ground and breathed into
his nostrils the breath of life, and the man became a living being . . . and
The Lord God took the man and put him in the Garden of Eden to work it
and take care of it.”(NIV)

                                                              45
                                      WORKING AT THE ASSIGNMENT

You were created to work. Your purpose is linked to your work.
