bondage. Take up work and jobs based on where you are going in life.

Types of Work

The correct concept of work sees work as anything you exact yourself
at to create your future, prepare for and/or fulfill your assignment,
create wealth, generate resources for life sustenance towards the
assignment, achieve your goals and fulfill your life purpose. Work is a
timeless principle for man on earth. This is the reason unemployment
is not just financial problem, it deteriorates the emotional well-being,
self-confidence and spiritual health of ‘the jobless’.

You don’t want to put your self in a position of joblessness. So, go out;
there is work.

                                                              48
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

It is noteworthy that the difference between working for survival and
working for assignment is in the mindset and perspective of the worker
and not necessarily in the exertion of work. Both the assignment
worker and the survival worker, most times are doing the same thing
but with different mental approaches. Thus, their life results are
different. Two different people can be employed in the same work,
doing the same thing. One with a survival mindset and the other with
an assignment mindset.

In today’s world, there is entrepreneurial work and intrapreneurial
work. Entrepreneurial work is work initiative taken by someone to
create or sell value to meet a felt need in others and thereby generate
profit. Entrepreneurship is when someone takes personal initiative,
starts up a venture or organisation, or partners with like-minded people
to meet an identified need in the market and make profit doing so.
Entrepreneurs manages resources, risk and opportunities to create a
business or company, to sell a product or service to a target market.
Founders of organisations (profit or non-profit) are generally
entrepreneurial workers. Entrepreneurial work is a great deal of hard-
work, because one has to deliver results without anyone to drive or
manage. Entrepreneurs must be self-driven workers.

Intrapreneurial work is using new and innovative ideas to advance an
existing organisation, thereby enhancing the organisation’s profitability
and generating rewards for yourself. Recently, more businesses are
engaging a model of intrapreneurship where workers in an organisation
determine how much they earn and how far they go by their unique
value addition and contribution to the organisational bottom-line.

                                                              49
                                      WORKING AT THE ASSIGNMENT

An intrapreneur enjoys the benefits of entrepreneurship within a larger
organisation, thereby absolving him of the risk associated with him
starting up a company. When an organisation systemically allows its
workers to apply an entrepreneurial mindset to their job within a
company, it s using intrapreneurial techniques. It is important to know
how to be an intrapreneur within an organisation and also important
for leaders to know how to develop an intrapreneurial mindset and not
merely an employee mindset in their workers.

Intrapreneurs are employees but not all employees are intrapreneurs.
Intrapreneurs are innovative people who engage entrepreneurial drive
and creativity to expand the profitability of an organisation where they
are employed, even though they are not the founders. It is important to
differentiate between employees who simply are employee-minded and
those who are intrapreneurs. Employee-minded people, many times,
are security seekers, who carry out task allotted to them in an
organisation and seeks a salary which should cover their needs. They
most times do not have self-initiative or vision, they do just enough to
stay employed, because they do not want to lose the job as it gives
them a source of livelihood. Intrapreneurs have a vision and they see
the opportunity to fulfill it while working in another person’s vision.
It is important to understand that both entrepreneurial and
intrapreneurial work is profitable. Fulfilling your assignment demands
that you either work in an existing organisation or start an
organisation. Starting up anything of value is a great deal of work and
involves a great amount of risk. It is not everyone that has developed
the capacity to succeed at entrepreneurial ventures.

                                                              50
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Some people in a misguided notion that they should not work for
another person or organisation but be ‘their own boss’, lie all day doing
