gives you the opportunity to learn and grow. It is gives the privilege of
having consistent income to build your financial future. It supplies
resources both tangible and intangible, to prepare and invest in your
life assignment. Both entrepreneurial and intrapreneurial work is good
at different phases of life. Thus, the scripture says, in all labor there is
profit, but idle chatter leads only to poverty. (Prov 14:23 NKJV)

On the other hand, working with a mere employee-mindset, which is
most times a mindset of servitude and survival through salary and
wages, is detrimental to destiny. What the recent emphasis on people
going into entrepreneurship and not being employed under someone
else should try to do is to damage is the unhealthy ‘employee mindset’
in people and not make it look as if everyone should leave their jobs
and go startup something. Statistically, 95% of business start-ups fail
and as a matter of fact, most people that start-up business, especially in
Africa, are not entrepreneurs but self-employed people.

Knowing the advantages of entrepreneurship versus intrapreneurship,
the difference between a business owner and a self-employed person
and the qualities to develop for different work types is outside the
scope of this book. Therefore, it is important go out of your way to do
a personal research on the details of each type of work and discover
which is best-suited for you.

                                                              51
                                      WORKING AT THE ASSIGNMENT

Work and Job

Understanding the concept of work thus makes us understand that
being employed at a job is not contrary to life assignment. In fact, it
could be necessary to discover one’s assignment, learn and develop
skills, prepare for one’s vision and even get finances to sustain oneself
while discovering, developing and fulfilling purpose. It could also bring
in some capital to contribute to funding one’s assignment. However,
working at a job (career, business or ministry) with a survival mentality
sucks life out of a destiny. It is good to get a good job, it is also much
better to also discover your life assignment. The two can run
concurrently. However, if the two clashes, your assignment is superior
to the good job.
Life would be more meaningful if people spent as much time
discovering, investing into and pursuing their life work as they spend
looking for jobs. The balance, has already established earlier, is that
discovering your Life Assignment and Life Work does not mean that
you may not have to take up a job. While paying bills, having food to
eat and meeting needs is not the essence of working in life, working to
make ends meet is a legitimate reason in today’s world although it is
not the ultimate reason. Therefore, as you work at a job to learn and
earn a sustenance, seek to discover your life work and start working
diligently at it.
Your life work, is the work you are doing in line with your life
assignment. This work is a lifetime venture and no employer can fire
you from it. Careers can collapse and people can lose jobs, but when
you discover your life work, you always have a reason to wake up and
exert yourself productively. Fulfillment comes when what you do daily
is aligned to your life work.

                                                              52
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

It is most crucial for those that have a job that is not specifically their
life assignment to still exert themselves in a work that is their life
assignment. This could be a for profit, non-profit, ministry-related
work or an investment portfolio you are building to enable you do the
things that matter to your life and destiny later. Get involved in
something that you know is the essence and purpose of your life while
you are still at that job that you know is not the entire essence of your
life.

Many Activities - One Task

Finally, on “Life Assignment and Work,” it is important to know that
there are many things one will do on earth. The concept of life
assignment is not an attempt to say that there is one singular thing that
you do with life, to the exclusion of every item in life. Some people
have erroneously thought that life assignment means that there is one
thing you will pursue and face in life. This misunderstanding has
become the undoing and failure of many ‘purposeful and assignment-
conscious fanatics’.

As usually said, one could fall into a ditch on either side of the road.
One extreme is found in those that pursue survival and security in life,
with no thought of the higher purpose of Life Assignment. The other
extreme is found in people who have become irresponsible and
unrealistic with everyday life and do nothing to make a decent living for
self-dependence in the name of pursuing something higher with their
lives.
There has been a noted trend of pragmatic irresponsibility with
working to meet up with the everyday expenditure and demands of life,
among those who seem to have a particular passion thay see as the
essence of their lives.

                                                              53
                                      WORKING AT THE ASSIGNMENT

There have been people who believe their life assignment is related to
a particular expression of art, music, sport, passion or spiritual ministry
and they literally become irresponsible in every other area of life except
the singular activity of that vocation. This in itself is a gross
misconception of life assignment. I was particularly pained once when
I met on the streets, one of my seniors in the university who we knew
to be very given to spiritual pursuits to the exclusion of academics and
regular work some years after I had graduated. He walked to me, gave
me a spiritual greeting and talked about how he came for a church
meeting in town and needed money to get back to his base. I respected
his spiritual passion, but I knew he could be as passionate for spiritual
things as he was and still take responsibility in other areas of life. I gave
him some money because I knew and trusted him.

The fact that one’s life assignment is to be a musician, does not mean
that such as person should only sing and sit on a musical instrument all
day. Life is a holistic system with many components. Your life
assignment is your life’s cutting edge, but it is not your life’s singular
activity. Going to school to study a course, learning a tradable skill,
volunteering in projects, developing streams of income, working at a
job, building and keeping healthy relationships, building and fending
for your family are integral parts of life. No structure stands sustainably
on one leg - life also stands on many legs.

A person may be called to be a musician, artist, sportsperson, gospel
minister etc. This may also be his/her life assignment. But that does
not mean that is the entirety of the activity he/she should do.

                                                              54
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

You should successfully study a course, work at a business, ministry or
organisation, build a family and do things that build your life
holistically to sustain you in carrying out the life assignment.

There have been people who believe they are called to be musicians,
who do not take their academics serious, do not take their finances
