                                                              56
                                 CHAPTER 6

             Understanding The Kingdom

God has an assignment for everything He created. Nature, spirits,
humans, all living things and inanimate objects are all created for
specific functions in God’s agenda. According to Col 1:16, for through
him God created everything in the heavenly realms and on earth. He made
the things we can see and the things we can't see such as thrones,
kingdoms, rulers, and authorities in the unseen world. Everything was
created through him and for him (NLT). Everything and everyone exist
for God’s purpose. Therefore, the assignment of everything and
everyone on earth is found in what God’s grand purpose on earth is.
God merely creates and delegates to each person, a role to fulfill in His
overall purpose. Thus, the understanding of Life-Assignment is elusive
until one thoroughly understands God’s Assignment. This chapter on
“Understanding the Kingdom of God” will clearly explain God’s
assignment, so you can thereby know your place and purpose in God’s
grand assignment.

God's Assignment - The Kingdom

God is the King and His Kingdom is established throughout all
eternity. God sits supreme in Heaven, from where He rules the
Kingdom. The reign of God is undisputed in heaven. It is only on earth
that the reign of God. The Kingdom of God, is in question, because
Man, His viceroy, lost the Kingdom.

                                                              57
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

The singular work of God on the earth is restoring the earth - the
world and all that is in it, to His Kingdom. The word ‘Kingdom’ means
‘king’s domain’. It is the domain where a kingdom rules or reigns. The
Kingdom of God is the realms of God’s reign.

The kingdom of God does not refer to a church or religion, it is the
governing influence of God over a territory, run by His principles,
impacted with His will, purpose and intents, and producing a people
who express His culture and reflect His nature. Thus, the Kingdom of
God is used to describe any territory, place, person, system,
organisation, business, or nation that is ruled under the recognition of
the Lordship of the Person of Jesus, by the principles of the Word of
God, and whose lives express a culture that depicts the character of
God. An individual, family, business, enterprise, institution, ministry,
political state, country, or territory can be the Kingdom of God. Thus,
Luke 17: 20 - 21 records, now when He was asked by the Pharisees when
the kingdom of God would come, He answered them and said, "The
kingdom of God does not come with observation; nor will they say,'See
here!' or 'See there!' For indeed, the kingdom of God is within you."
Luke 17:20-21 NKJV.

The Kingdom of God is intangible and it is inherently contained,
transmitted, expressed and promulgated by persons and systems. Your
purpose on earth is to propagate God’s Kingdom. Your “Life
Assignment” is to carry out a task that God has given you in a sphere
of life, nd by so doing impose, promulgate and establish God’s
Kingdom; His Lordship, dominion, rule and reign, in your world.

                                                              58
                                    UNDERSTANDING THE KINGDOM

God's Assignment - The Kingdom

When people understand the great Kingdom Assignment of God, they
become purposeful in life. They cease to be confused about why they
exist and know what to do with their lives.

God is the Creator of all things therefore, He has the right to rule over
all. Thus, the Kingdom of God spans all things, places and realms in
eternity. However, not all persons, places, systems and things are under
the experiential reign of God through submission and compliance to
His will and ways.

This is aptly captured by Ps 115:16 when it says, the heavens belong to
the Lord, but he has given the earth to all humanity. God is King over all
things and kingdoms, but He benevolently delegated the kingdom of
the earth to man. Thus, all happening on the earth are not as a result of
God’s sovereignty, but man’s determination. This explains the fact that
the many wrong things happening in different sectors of nations,
communities, people’s lives are not God’s making. They are as a result
of the fact that the Kingdom of God is not reigning in those areas.

Matt 6:10, says, thy kingdom come. Thy will be done in earth, as it is in
heaven. Thus, God’s Kingdom comes upon an individual, system or
territory when His will is being done therein. Such a person, place or
system becomes an outpost of heaven. As currently, God’s will is not
fully done over nations, societies, institutions, politics, education,
churches, economies, homes and individuals, the “Life assignment” of
every kingdom citizen is to bring an assigned sphere under the
Kingdom reign.

                                                              59
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

Do you know that many of the things you have been complaining
