The Kingdom Story

God is the King of the Kingdom. When Satan, led some created beings,
to rebel and set up a parallel kingdom, he and his cohorts were sent on
exile, plunged into eternal darkness and damned to destruction. All
these predated the existence of man.

Therefore, the book of Genesis in the Bible opens with a record of God
re-instating a kingdom on the earth with man as a regent under God.
The earth was an outpost of Heaven and God and man, connected to
God by the Holy Spirit, was to rule over the Kingdom of the earth. He
was to express God’s will, culture, principles and nature, in the world
by the Spirit of God in Him. Man was the crown king over the
kingdoms of the world and he was to rule under the authority of God,
His King.

When Satan told man to disobey God and carry out his instruction to
eat the fruit of knowledge of good and evil. It was not merely an issue
of eating fruits and the repercussions of eating. It was a kingdom clash,
one of the principles of the kingdom is that ‘ . . . to whom you present
yourselves slaves to obey, you are that one's slaves whom you obey . . .’
(Rom 6:16).

                                                              60
                                    UNDERSTANDING THE KINGDOM

Man, the king, has become the slave and the slave, satan, has become
king through guile. Prov 30: 21 - 22 mentions four things that is
