the life journey to raise the banner of the Kingdom of God in those
spheres(s).

                                                              66
                                 CHAPTER 7

                    Fulfilling Purpose

The most important thing you can do in life is to pursue and fulfil
God’s purpose for you. After salvation, the most important discovery
in life is the purpose for which you were created and saved.

Living Purposefully

This is the reason it is important to live by all Kingdom principles; add
those that make for purpose fulfillment to those that make for wealth,
prosperity and material success.
Purpose is primarily a mindset, an understanding, an attitude towards
life and all life activities that seeks, factors how to and actively does
things to advance God’s Kingdom in any sphere you find yourself,
because you believe that is the reason you are positioned there.
Purpose is an attitude towards that understands the sphere of the
Kingdom that one has been assigned to take for Christ and engages in
every life activity with that singular goal in mind.
When you make every decision, take every step and do everything with
fulfilling your Kingdom as the priority viewpoint you are walking in
purpose. Purpose is not a destination or an event, it is a mindset.
Everything you do as your contribution and partnership with God to
fulfill your discovered assignment is walking in line with God’s purpose
for your life.

                                                              67
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

For this reason, schooling could be done in purpose or out of purpose,
building a business could be done in purpose or out of purpose, getting
married could be in purpose or out of purpose. Working at a job could
be in purpose or out of purpose. For instance, if a person’s life
assignment is to ignite a spiritual revival that will lead to a mass
entrance of individuals into God’s kingdom through evangelism and
such a person is working in a bank, that person is not living according
to God’s purpose. If a person’s life assignment is to build an
educational institution that will save, mentor and build as many as will
be part of the system and such as person takes a job as a full-time staff
in a church or pastor, diligently working to ‘serve God’, such a person
is out of purpose.
Purpose is determined by the manufacturer, it is God who determines
the role he wants you to play in His Kingdom. Do not be brainwashed
into thinking some roles are more spiritual than others. If the role is
from God, it is spiritual even if it is on a secular platform.

Types of Purpose

God has an eternal purpose He is working out and this purpose is His
Kingdom. Eph 3:11 shows that we are all called according to the eternal
purpose which He purposed in Christ Jesus our Lord. God’s purpose is
the advancement of Kingdom and every believer has a sub-assignment
within God’s Kingdom as their individual purpose.

God’s purpose can be seen from two perspectives:

                                                              68
                                             FULFILLING PURPOSE

1. The Generic Purpose of All Believers - God’s general purpose for
believer includes the assignments that are general to every child of God
irrespective of their individual spheres of callings and platforms.
(i) Kingdom Advancement through evangelism and discipleship of
persons, institutions, territories, nations (Matt. 28: 19 -20). Every child
of God should be involved in evangelism and discipleship irrespective
of whether they are called to the five-fold ministry or not.
(ii) Kingdom culture alignment of persons, institutions, territories,
nations (Rev. 11: 15). Every child of God must be involved in aligning
the culture of their spheres of influence, neighborhood and
communities to God through godly representation in daily life. This
involves challenging norms that are ungodly, addressing vices and
mindsets contrary to God. This is the correctional ministry of the
church against all that is evil in the world. You have a purpose in the
Kingdom to stand for what is right and to straighten out the culture of
your community.
(iii) Worship of the King (Rev. 4: 11). Every child of God has a
purpose to worship God and raise the banner of His name.
(iv) Glorifying King through our Results. (Matt. 5: 16,John. 15: 8)
Every believer has the duty to bring glory to God through good works,
success, and superior results over the world system etc.

2. The Specific Purpose of Each Believer - Each believer has a specific
platform where he is most suited for advancing God’s Kingdom.
Purpose discovery as popularly taught is actually the discovery of the
platform where you are meant to carry out God’s purpose for your life.

                                                              69
                                             THE LIFE ASSIGNMENT

In Jer. 1: 5 - 10, we see that Jeremiah had a specific purpose in the
prophetic office. For someone else, it may be in education, finance,
politics, media etc.
A believer can have a Kingdom purpose to fulfill in the following
spheres of influence. Some may have influence in more than one sphere
due to their Kingdom positioning. The list of spheres of Kingdom
purpose is endless however, they have been recently categorised in
seven categories:

1. Government/Governance - Politics, Law, Military, Civil Service,
etc
2. Media -- Writing, TV Shows, Journalism, News, Information,
Broadcasting, Social Media.
3. Finance/Business/Economy - Banking, Corporations, Commerce
etc.
4. Arts and Entertainment - Music, Drama, Comedy, Fashion, etc.
5. Education
6. Family and Relationships
7. Religion - Church and Para-church

Prayerfully discover where you are called to play a role for God. Know
what you want to achieve for your Kingdom in that sphere and go all
out to fulfill this task. You are always walking in God’s purpose for you
life.

